      "title": "DoJ declines to reopen investigation into former Fed chair Jay Powell",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/oct/02/doj-fed-chair-jerome-powell-investigation",
      "description": "<p>Kevin Warsh’s predecessor had been investigated over cost overruns related to central bank renovation project</p><p>The US ⁠justice department is not reopening a criminal investigation into former Federal Reserve chair <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/business/jerome-powell\">Jerome Powell</a> ⁠for cost overruns ⁠related ​to the central bank’s building renovation project, a department spokesperson said on Friday.</p><p>Attorney general <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/todd-blanche\">Todd ⁠Blanche</a> – in comments to <a href=\"https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-10-02/doj-not-reopening-criminal-probe-into-fed-s-powell-blanche-says\">Bloomberg News</a>, which first reported the development – said he has not ruled out ⁠continuing to look into the project’s oversight and potentially take ​action if evidence of ‌wrongdoing came to ‌light.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/oct/02/doj-fed-chair-jerome-powell-investigation\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-02T22:32:21"
    },
    {
      "title": "US justice department will not reopen criminal probe of Fed’s Jay Powell",
